    },
    "body": "**Problem:** Wallet encryption and passphrase changes can report success after a database write fails.\r\nInitial encryption can continue without a persisted master key, passphrase changes can update memory but not disk, and descriptor encryption can commit mixed plaintext and encrypted key records that prevent the wallet from loading.\r\nThese paths require a local database failure and are not remotely triggerable (database failures often require operator recovery regardless).\r\n\r\n**Fix:** Check each write before updating memory or committing encryption.\r\nFailed attempts preserve the previous key records and passphrase state so the operation can be retried.\r\nFault-injection tests [characterize](https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/35260) all three failures before the focused fixes, to make it clear how the fixes change previous behavior.",
